  i.e. omega_c >= 6.482e-15 rad/s.

  g02 scans down to 2.000e-15, which is 3.24x BELOW that bound.  At that omega_c the
  framework's own gate leaves the inner-disk star  Re G = 0.087  -- galaxies keep
  9% of their MOND boost, i.e. the RAR is destroyed.  So the headline 4.54% is
  evaluated at an omega_c the framework has already excluded.
  [FAIL] A1 the claim's 'window bottom edge' is NOT the galactic-survival bound -- it sits a factor 3+ below it, at an omega_c where the framework's own gate switches galaxies off   (g02 lo = 2.000e-15 against the anchor's 6.482e-15 (3.24x); Re G at Omega_gal,max would be 0.087 -- FAILING THIS IS THE REFUTATION OF THE CLAIM'S STATED WINDOW)

