====================================================================================================
  A3  THREE POINTS ARE NOT A SCAN -- |S-1| is non-monotonic in omega_c
====================================================================================================

  |S-1| -> 0 as omega_c -> 0 (gate shuts on BOTH trajectories) and -> 0.10% as
  omega_c -> inf (gate open on both).  It therefore PEAKS in between: the true maximum over all
  omega_c is 7.95% at omega_c = 7.659e-16 rad/s -- which lies BELOW g02's own 'lo', so the
  three sampled points cannot establish 'the largest departure' even inside the stated interval.
  (Inside g02's interval the max is 4.53%, at its bottom edge -- true, but shown
  here by a 6001-point grid, not by the three evaluations OMC = dict(lo, committed, hi).)
  [FAIL] A3 the claim's 'exhaustive scan over the parameter's whole allowed window' is three function evaluations of a NON-MONOTONIC function whose global maximum lies outside them   (global peak 7.95% at 7.659e-16, below g02's lo 2.000e-15 -- FAILING THIS RECORDS THAT 3 POINTS DID NOT ESTABLISH THE MAXIMUM)

